# Who reviews what in the guide.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, and a match replaces the owners rather
# than adding to them, so every rule below names @rladies/website too:
# they own the build and the site itself, and were the sole owner before
# these rules existed.
#
# The point of the rest is that a page about how a team works should be
# reviewed by that team. Adding a section here is the easiest way to get
# the right people onto a pull request automatically, rather than
# remembering to tag them.

*                                       @rladies/website

# Global team operations: one rule per team that runs the thing described
content/global-team/monitoring/         @rladies/chapter-activity @rladies/website
content/global-team/onboarding/         @rladies/chapter-onboarding @rladies/website
content/global-team/meetup/             @rladies/meetup-pro @rladies/website
